From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:41:44 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 100/103] Translate pages, and agents can guide the person
 through a site

The site controls get Translate to <your language> (Chromium's built-in
Google Translate, free) and back. Over MCP: translate_page, and
highlight / wait_for_user / clear_highlights, a ring with a note by the
element for each step, so an agent shows the way while the person does
it. They change nothing on the page, so read-only access may use them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
